WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.800
Hugging Face.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.028
Almost every open model you'll use arrives through it.

3
00:00:05.028 --> 00:00:06.600
Here's how to think about it.

4
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.133
Hugging Face is two things fused together.

5
00:00:10.433 --> 00:00:18.167
At the bottom, the Hub: hundreds of thousands of pretrained models, datasets, and model cards behind a git-like API.

6
00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:22.067
On top, the transformers library, which loads and runs them.

7
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.900
And your code picks one of two levels to call it.

8
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.520
Level one is pipeline.

9
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:33.133
It wraps preprocessing, model, and postprocessing in one line, perfect for prototyping.

10
00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:39.933
Level two is the Auto classes, where you tokenize, run the forward pass, and handle the logits yourself.

11
00:00:40.233 --> 00:00:42.967
You need that for batching, custom heads, and serving.

12
00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.900
It's the same math underneath.

13
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.933
Here's the chain pipeline hides.

14
00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:49.467
Raw text goes in.

15
00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:51.900
The tokenizer turns it into tensors.

16
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.367
The model runs the forward pass and returns logits.

17
00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:58.229
Softmax converts them into probabilities.

18
00:00:58.229 --> 00:01:00.167
Now you can inspect every step.

19
00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:02.633
Here are both levels.

20
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:06.142
First an alias for the classification head class.

21
00:01:06.142 --> 00:01:08.500
Level one is a single pipeline call.

22
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.260
Level two loads tokenizer and model from the same name.

23
00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.267
They must match.

24
00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:17.100
Then we tokenize, run the model, and softmax the logits.

25
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.567
Here are both levels.

26
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:22.783
First, the alias picks a classification head.

27
00:01:22.783 --> 00:01:25.700
Level one is a single line: build a pipeline.

28
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.460
Level two loads tokenizer and model from the same name.

29
00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:30.467
They must match.

30
00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:34.300
Then we tokenize, run the model, and softmax the logits.

31
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.900
Here's how it plays out.

32
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.433
You prototype note triage with pipeline in an afternoon.

33
00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:45.667
In the service, you use the Auto level: load once, batch thirty two notes per pass.

34
00:01:45.967 --> 00:01:51.733
You keep the raw logits, and send anything below zero point seven confidence to human review.

35
00:01:52.933 --> 00:01:53.703
Let's recap.

36
00:01:53.703 --> 00:01:57.167
Hugging Face is the Hub plus the transformers library.

37
00:01:57.467 --> 00:02:01.100
Use pipeline to prototype, and Auto classes for control.

38
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.998
Always match tokenizer and checkpoint.

39
00:02:03.998 --> 00:02:05.433
Next up: the encoder.
